  "releaseNotes": "0.7.0: Core client integration\n- AddImageAssetWithAutoAdjustment now accepts StateReference for the state field name. Strings remain usable through implicit conversion, but empty names, whitespace, and backticks are rejected.\n- Core request serialization now preserves derived AssetState properties alongside image asset references, including asset state items in combined JevMessage content.\n- The core client now supports opt-in long context and optional strict model validation. Automatic model selection uses JevModel.Latest, including Box questions; explicit models remain unchanged and Box questions require jev-1.14.0 or later.\n- Long context beyond the default 64 KB is slower and less accurate. The bundled known-model list may lag the TypeSafe API.",
